= #text("The Value of Science / 科学的价值")

#html.p(id: "en-S001")[#text("From time to time, people suggest to me that scientists ought to give more consideration to social problems—especially that they should be more responsible in considering the impact of science upon society. This same suggestion is made to all the other scientists, and it seems to me that we do think about these problems from time to time, but we don't put full-time effort on them—the reason being that we know we don't have any magic formula for solving problems, that social problems are very much harder than scientific ones, and that we usually don't get anywhere when we do think about them.")]

#zh(id: "S001")[#text("人们不时地向我建议，科学家应该更多地考虑社会问题，尤其是在考虑科学对社会的影响时，他们应该更负责任。对所有其他科学家都提出了同样的建议，在我看来，我们确实时不时地思考这些问题，但我们没有全时的精力 -- 原因是我们知道我们没有任何解决问题的神奇公式，社会问题比科学问题更难，当我们思考它们时，我们通常不会有任何进展。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S002")[#text("I believe that a scientist looking at non-scientific problems is just as dumb as the next guy—and when he talks about a non-scientific matter, he will sound as naïve as anyone untrained in the matter. Since the question of the value of science is not a scientific subject, this talk is dedicated to proving my point—by example.")]

#zh(id: "S002")[#text("我相信，研究非科学问题的科学家和其他人一样愚蠢 -- 当他谈论非科学问题时，他会听起来像任何未经过这方面训练的人一样天真。由于科学的价值问题不是科学主题，因此本演讲致力于通过实例证明我的观点。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S003")[#text("The first way in which science is of value is familiar to everyone. It is that scientific knowledge enables us to do all kinds of things and to make all kinds of things. Of course if we make good things, it is not only to the credit of science; it is also to the credit of the moral choice which led us to good work. Scientific knowledge is an enabling power to do either good or bad—but it does not carry instructions on how to use it. Such power has evident value—even though the power may be negated by what one does.")]

#zh(id: "S003")[#text("科学的第一种价值体现，是人人都熟悉的。正是科学知识使我们能够做各种各样的事情，使各种各样的事情。当然，如果我们做出了好东西，那不仅是对科学的信任; 这也是对道德选择的信任，这使我们做出了好的工作。科学知识是一种使人能够做好事或坏事的力量，但它不带有如何使用它的指示。这种权力具有明显的价值 -- 即使这种权力可能被一个人所做的事情所否定。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S004")[#text("I learned a way of expressing this common human problem on a trip to Honolulu. In a Buddhist temple there, the man in charge explained a little bit about the Buddhist religion for tourists, and then ended his talk by telling them he had something to say to them that they would never forget—and I have never forgotten it. It was a proverb of the Buddhist religion:")]

#zh(id: "S004")[#text("在去檀香山的旅行中，我学会了一种表达这种常见的人类问题的方法。在那里的一座佛教寺庙里，负责人为游客解释了一点佛教信仰，然后结束了他的谈话，告诉他们他有话要对他们说，他们永远不会忘记 -- 我也永远不会忘记。这是佛教的一句谚语:")]

#html.p(id: "en-S005")[#text("“To every man is given the key to the gates of heaven; the same key opens the gates of hell.”")]

#zh(id: "S005")[#text("“每个人都有打开天堂之门的钥匙; 同样的钥匙打开地狱之门。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S006")[#text("What then, is the value of the key to heaven? It is true that if we lack clear instructions that determine which is the gate to heaven and which the gate to hell, the key may be a dangerous object to use, but it obviously has value. How can we enter heaven without it?")]

#zh(id: "S006")[#text("那么，通往天堂的钥匙的价值是什么？诚然，如果我们缺乏明确的指令来确定哪个是通往天堂的大门，哪个是通往地狱之门，那么钥匙可能是一个危险的对象，但它显然具有价值。没有它，我们怎么能进天堂？")]

#html.p(id: "en-S007")[#text("The instructions, also, would be of no value without the key. So it is evident that, in spite of the fact that science could produce enormous horror in the world, it is of value because it can produce something.")]

#zh(id: "S007")[#text("此外，如果没有密钥，这些说明也将毫无用处。因此，很明显，尽管科学可以在世界上产生巨大的恐怖，但它是有价值的，因为它可以产生一些东西。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S008")[#text("Another value of science is the fun called intellectual enjoyment which some people get from reading and learning and thinking about it, and which others get from working in it. This is a very real and important point and one which is not considered enough by those who tell us it is our social responsibility to reflect on the impact of science on society.")]

#zh(id: "S008")[#text("科学的另一个价值是一种叫做智力享受的乐趣，有些人从阅读、学习和思考中获得这种乐趣，而另一些人则从工作中获得这种乐趣。这是一个非常真实和重要的观点，那些告诉我们反思科学对社会的影响是我们的社会责任的人认为这一点还不够。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S009")[#text("Is this mere personal enjoyment of value to society as a whole? No! But it is also a responsibility to consider the value of society itself. Is it, in the last analysis, to arrange things so that people can enjoy things? If so, the enjoyment of science is as important as anything else.")]

#zh(id: "S009")[#text("这仅仅是个人对整个社会的价值享受吗？不！但考虑社会本身的价值也是一种责任。在最后的分析中，是为了安排事物以便人们可以享受事物吗？如果是这样的话，享受科学和其他任何东西一样重要。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S010")[#text("But I would like not to underestimate the value of the world view which is the result of scientific effort. We have been led to imagine all sorts of things infinitely more marvelous than the imaginings of poets and dreamers of the past. It shows that the imagination of nature is far, far greater than the imagination of man. For instance, how much more remarkable it is for us all to be stuck—half of us upside down—by a mysterious attraction, to a spinning ball that has been swinging in space for billions of years, than to be carried on the back of an elephant supported on a tortoise swimming in a bottomless sea.")]

#zh(id: "S010")[#text("但我不想低估世界观的价值，这是科学努力的结果。我们被引导去想象各种各样的事物，比过去的诗人和梦想家的想象更加奇妙。它表明，自然的想象力远远大于人类的想象力。例如，对于我们所有人来说，被一个神秘的吸引力所吸引，被一个在太空中摆动了数十亿年的旋转球所吸引，而不是被背在无底大海中游泳的乌龟支撑的大象背上。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S011")[#text("I have thought about these things so many times alone that I hope you will excuse me if I remind you of some thoughts that I am sure you have all had—or this type of thought—which no one could ever have had in the past, because people then didn't have the information we have about the world today.")]

#zh(id: "S011")[#text("我独自思考过这些事情很多次，我希望你能原谅我，如果我提醒你一些想法，我相信你们都有过 -- 或者这种类型的想法 -- 在过去没有人有过，因为那时人们没有我们今天所拥有的关于世界的信息。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S012")[#text("For instance, I stand at the seashore, alone, and start to think. There are the rushing waves…mountains of molecules, each stupidly minding its own business…trillions apart…yet forming white surf in unison.")]

#zh(id: "S012")[#text("例如，我独自站在海边，开始思考。有汹涌的海浪…… 成山的分子，每个分子都愚蠢地想着自己的事…… 相隔数万亿…… 却一致地形成白色的海浪。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S013")[#text("Ages on ages…before any eyes could see…year after year…thunderously pounding the shore as now. For whom, for what?…on a dead planet, with no life to entertain.")]

#zh(id: "S013")[#text("岁月悠悠……在任何眼睛能够看见之前……年复一年……如今般轰鸣着拍打着海岸。为了谁，为了什么？……在一个死寂的星球上，没有任何生命可供消遣。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S014")[#text("Never at rest…tortured by energy…wasted prodigiously by the sun…poured into space. A mite makes the sea roar.")]

#zh(id: "S014")[#text("永不停息……为能量所折磨……被太阳无情地消耗殆尽……最终倾泻于宇宙之中。一只螨虫让大海咆哮。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S015")[#text("Deep in the sea, all molecules repeat the patterns of one another till complex new ones are formed. They make others like themselves…and a new dance starts.")]

#zh(id: "S015")[#text("在深海之中，所有的分子都以相同的模式不断重复，直至形成复杂的全新结构。他们让别人变得和自己一样……于是，一场新的舞蹈就此展开。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S016")[#text("Growing in size and complexity…living things, masses of atoms, DNA, protein…dancing a pattern ever more intricate.")]

#zh(id: "S016")[#text("不断增长的规模与复杂性……生命体、原子团、DNA、蛋白质……在演绎着愈发精妙的律动。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S017")[#text("Out of the cradle onto the dry land…here it is standing…atoms with consciousness…matter with curiosity.")]

#zh(id: "S017")[#text("从摇篮走向干燥的大地……它就在这里伫立着……拥有意识的原子……充满好奇心的物质。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S018")[#text("Stands at the sea…wonders at wondering…I…a universe of atoms…an atom in the universe.")]

#zh(id: "S018")[#text("伫立于海边……惊叹于这惊叹本身……我……一个由原子构成的宇宙……宇宙中的一个原子。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S019")[#text("The same thrill, the same awe and mystery, come again and again when we look at any problem deeply enough. With more knowledge comes deeper, more wonderful mystery, luring one on to penetrate deeper still. Never concerned that the answer may prove disappointing, but with pleasure and confidence we turn over each new stone to find unimagined strangeness leading on to more wonderful questions and mysteries—certainly a grand adventure!")]

#zh(id: "S019")[#text("当我们足够深入地看待任何问题时，同样的激动，同样的敬畏和神秘会一次又一次地出现。随着知识的积累，神秘愈发深邃而迷人，诱使人不断深入探究。从来没有担心答案可能会令人失望，但我们愉快和信心地翻过每一块新石头，发现无法想象的奇怪之处，导致更多精彩的问题和奥秘-当然是一次盛大的冒险!")]

#html.p(id: "en-S020")[#text("It is true that few unscientific people have this particular type of religious experience. Our poets do not write about it; our artists do not try to portray this remarkable thing. I don't know why. Is no one inspired by our present picture of the universe? This value of science remains unsung by singers: you are reduced to hearing not a song or poem, but an evening lecture about it. This is not yet a scientific age.")]

#zh(id: "S020")[#text("确实，很少有非科学信仰者会经历这种特定类型的宗教体验。我们的诗人不为此作诗；我们的艺术家也不试图描绘这非凡之物。我不知道为什么。难道就没有人被我们目前对宇宙的认知所启发吗？科学的这种价值仍然是歌手所不知道的: 你只听一首歌或一首诗，而是一场关于它的晚间讲座。这还不是一个科学的时代。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S021")[#text("Perhaps one of the reasons for this silence is that you have to know how to read the music. For instance, the scientific article may say, “The radioactive phosphorus content of the cerebrum of the rat decreases to one-half in a period of two weeks.” Now what does that mean?")]

#zh(id: "S021")[#text("或许，造成这种沉默的原因之一在于，你必须懂得如何“读懂”乐谱。例如，科学文章可能会说，“大鼠大脑的放射性磷含量在两周内减少到一半。” 这意味着什么？")]

#html.p(id: "en-S022")[#text("It means that phosphorus that is in the brain of a rat—and also in mine, and yours—is not the same phosphorus that was there two weeks ago. It means the atoms that are in the brain are being replaced: the ones that were there before have gone away.")]

#zh(id: "S022")[#text("这意味着，老鼠大脑中的磷——同样也存在于我的大脑和你的大脑中——并不是两周前那里的磷。这意味着大脑中的原子正在被替换：原先存在的那些原子已经消失了。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S023")[#text("So what is this mind of ours: what are these atoms with consciousness? Last week's potatoes! That is what now can remember what was going on in my mind a year ago—a mind which has long ago been replaced.")]

#zh(id: "S023")[#text("那么，我们的思想是什么: 这些具有意识的原子是什么？上周的土豆！这就是现在可以记起一年前我脑海中发生的事情-一种早已被取代的思想。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S024")[#text("That is what it means when one discovers how long it takes for the atoms of the brain to be replaced by other atoms, to note that the thing which I call my individuality is only a pattern or dance. The atoms come into my brain, dance a dance, then go out—always new atoms but always doing the same dance, remembering what the dance was yesterday.")]

#zh(id: "S024")[#text("这就是当一个人发现大脑的原子被其他原子取代需要多长时间时的意思，注意到我称之为我的个性的东西只是一种模式或舞蹈。原子进入我的大脑，跳舞，然后出去-总是新的原子，但总是做同样的舞蹈，记住昨天的舞蹈是什么。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S025")[#text("When we read about this in the newspaper, it says, “The scientist says that this discovery may have importance in the cure of cancer.” The paper is only interested in the use of the idea, not the idea itself. Hardly anyone can understand the importance of an idea, it is so remarkable. Except that, possibly, some children catch on. And when a child catches on to an idea like that, we have a scientist.")]

#zh(id: "S025")[#text("当我们在报纸上读到这一点时，它说: “科学家说这一发现可能对治愈癌症有重要意义。” 这篇论文只对这个想法的使用感兴趣，而不是这个想法本身。几乎没有人能够理解一个想法的重要性，它实在是太非凡了。只不过，也许有些孩子会明白。而当一个孩子领悟到这样的想法时，我们就拥有了一位科学家。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S026")[#text("It is very curious that in our society, while we have an interest in all sorts of things, and we have an appreciation for all sorts of things, we have a complete ignorance and a complete lack of appreciation of science. We are not teaching science in a way that is good for the development of the human mind. We are not teaching it so that it is a part of the human, of the general culture. We are not teaching it so that men can feel that they have some understanding of the world in which they live.")]

#zh(id: "S026")[#text("非常奇怪的是，在我们的社会中，尽管我们对各种事物都感兴趣，并且对各种事物都有欣赏，但我们却完全无知，完全缺乏对科学的欣赏。我们没有以有利于人类思维发展的方式教授科学。我们并不是为了使其成为人类整体文化的一部分而对其进行教授。我们教授它，并不是为了让男性觉得自己对所处的世界有了一点了解。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S027")[#text("The last of the values of science, which I want to talk about, is a little more indirect, but not much. The scientist has a lot of experience with ignorance and doubt and uncertainty, and this experience is of very great importance, I think. When a scientist doesn't know the answer to a problem, he is ignorant. When he has a hunch as to what the result is, he is uncertain. And when he is pretty darn sure of what the result is going to be, he is in some doubt. We have found it of paramount importance that in order to progress we must recognize our ignorance and leave room for doubt. Scientific knowledge is a body of statements of varying degrees of certainty—some most unsure, some nearly sure, none absolutely certain.")]

#zh(id: "S027")[#text("我想谈的科学价值的最后一项，虽然稍显间接，但也相差无几。科学家在面对无知、怀疑与不确定性方面积累了丰富的经验，而我认为，这种经验具有极为重要的意义。当一位科学家不知道某个问题的答案时，他就处于无知的状态。当他隐约觉得结果会怎样时，他仍然感到不确定。而当他几乎可以肯定结果会是什么时，他又有些拿不准了。我们发现至关重要的是，为了进步，我们必须认识到我们的无知，并留下怀疑的余地。科学知识是一系列不同程度的确定性陈述 -- 有些是最不确定的，有些是几乎确定的，没有一个是绝对确定的。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S028")[#text("Now, we scientists are used to this, and we take it for granted that it is perfectly consistent to be unsure, that it is possible to live and not know. But I don't know whether everyone realizes this is true. Our freedom to doubt was born out of a struggle against authority in the early days of science. It was a very deep and strong struggle: permit us to question—to doubt—to not be sure. I think that it is important that we do not forget this struggle and thus perhaps lose what we have gained. Herein lies a responsibility to society.")]

#zh(id: "S028")[#text("现在，我们科学家已经习惯了这一点，我们理所当然地认为不确定是完全一致的，有可能生活而不知道。但我不知道大家是否都意识到这一点。我们的怀疑自由是在科学早期与权威的斗争中产生的。这是一场非常深刻和强烈的斗争: 允许我们质疑 -- 怀疑 -- 不确定。我认为重要的是，我们不要忘记这场斗争，从而可能失去我们所获得的。这正是我们对社会的责任所在。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S029")[#text("We are all sad when we think of the wondrous potentialities human beings seem to have, as contrasted with their small accomplishments. Again and again people have thought that we could do much better. They of the past saw in the nightmare of their times a dream for the future. We, of their future, see that their dreams, in certain ways surpassed, have in many ways remained dreams. The hopes for the future today are, in good share, those of yesterday.")]

#zh(id: "S029")[#text("当我们想到人类似乎拥有的奇妙潜力，与他们的小成就形成对比时，我们都很难过。人们一次又一次地认为，我们本可以做得更好。过去的他们在他们时代的噩梦中看到了未来的梦想。我们，他们的未来，看到他们的梦想，在某些方面超越，在许多方面仍然是梦想。今日对未来的期望，在很大程度上仍是昨日的期望。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S030")[#text("Education, for good and evil")]

#zh(id: "S030")[#text("教育，有善亦有恶")]

#html.p(id: "en-S031")[#text("Once some thought that the possibilities people had were not developed because most of those people were ignorant. With education universal, could all men be Voltaires? Bad can be taught at least as efficiently as good. Education is a strong force, but for either good or evil.")]

#zh(id: "S031")[#text("曾经有人认为人们的可能性没有被开发出来，因为大多数人都是无知的。在教育普及的情况下，所有人都能成为伏尔泰吗？坏的东西至少可以像好的东西一样高效地被传授。教育是一股强大的力量，但它既可以为善，也可以为恶。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S032")[#text("Communication between nations must promote understanding—so went another dream. But the communication systems are dominated by a noisy disharmony of advertisers and reviewers and commentators and critics. Communication is a strong force, but for either good or evil.")]

#zh(id: "S032")[#text("国与国之间的交流必须促进理解 -- 另一个梦想也是如此。但是，广告商和评论家，评论员和评论家的嘈杂不和谐主导了通信系统。沟通是一股强大的力量，但它既可以带来善，也可能导致恶。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S033")[#text("The applied sciences should free men of material problems at least. Medicine controls diseases. And the record here seems all to the good. Yet there are some patiently working today to create great plagues and poisons for use in warfare tomorrow.")]

#zh(id: "S033")[#text("应用科学至少应当使人们摆脱物质上的困扰。药物控制疾病。而这里的记录似乎一切良好。然而，今天有一些人耐心地工作，创造巨大的瘟疫和毒药，供明天的战争使用。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S034")[#text("Nearly everybody dislikes war. Our dream today is peace. In peace, man can develop best the enormous possibilities he seems to have. But maybe future men will find that peace, too, can be good and bad. Perhaps peaceful men will drink out of boredom. Then perhaps drink will become the great problem which seems to dwarf all others. Then, perhaps, they will search for solutions to this problem, when we have found that it is a thing of the past.")]

#zh(id: "S034")[#text("几乎人人都厌恶战争。我们今天的梦想是和平。在和平的环境中，人类能够最好地发挥其看似无穷无尽的潜能。但也许未来的人会发现和平，同样，可以是好的也可以是坏的。也许那些性情平和的人会因无聊而饮酒。然后，也许喝酒将成为使所有其他人相形见war的大问题。然后，也许，当我们发现这个问题已经成为过去时，他们会寻找解决方案。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S035")[#text("Always these things, the hopes of yesterday, were ideas which assumed that the solution of a problem was only to find a solution. But the solution may be just as complicated as the problem. The solution may be a thing that we can't accept. But we go on, trying to solve problems. We are not very careful, though, to notice that we are not succeeding.")]

#zh(id: "S035")[#text("总是这些事情，昨天的希望，是想法，假设解决问题只是找到一个解决方案。但解决方案可能与问题本身一样复杂。解决方案可能是一件我们无法接受的事情。但我们仍在继续，努力解决问题。然而，我们往往不够留心，以至于没有意识到自己并未取得成功。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S036")[#text("We are trying to do it, as we have always done, by having some fellows with ideas, some with power, lead us. And we are falling into the same old traps. We are not today, in the same high state of expectation of a new era of smoothly developing and improving human affairs that we were, say, in 1919. We have seen that the hopes of the past have not been realized, and we are not so enthusiastic about the hopes of the future.")]

#zh(id: "S036")[#text("我们正在努力做到这一点，就像我们一直做的那样，让一些有想法的人，一些有权力的人来领导我们。我们陷入了同样的陷阱。今天，我们并不像1919年那样，对一个平稳发展和改善人类事务的新时代抱有很高的期望。我们已经看到，过去的希望没有实现，我们对未来的希望也没有那么热情。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S037")[#text("We are particularly sad because we see that we have not made much progress. We have a little bit of a new problem. We have a new force, a new power, which is so great that we are not sure how to handle it. We are not sure how to control it. And we are not sure that we can control it. This is the power of science. And it is the power that gives us all the trouble today.")]

#zh(id: "S037")[#text("我们感到格外难过，因为我们意识到自己并没有取得多大进展。我们遇到了一点新问题。我们拥有一种新的力量，一种如此强大的力量，以至于我们尚不确定该如何应对。我们不确定如何控制它。而且我们也不确定能否将其控制住。这就是科学的力量。而正是这种力量，给我们带来了如今的所有麻烦。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S038")[#text("We are, all of us, in a difficult position. We are, all of us, trying to do our best. And we are, all of us, in some way, I think, failing.")]

#zh(id: "S038")[#text("我们所有人都处于困境中。我们所有人都在努力做到最好。我认为，在某种程度上，我们所有人都失败了。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S039")[#text("I am sorry to have to tell you this, but I do not see any easy solution. I do not see any possibility of our being able to solve the problems of the world in the way that we have, in the past, solved some of our problems.")]

#zh(id: "S039")[#text("我很抱歉要告诉你这一点，但我没有看到任何简单的解决方案。我看不出我们有任何可能以我们过去解决一些问题的方式来解决世界问题。")]

#html.p(id: "en-S040")[#text("What should we do about it? I think, as scientists, we have a special responsibility. I think that we have a responsibility to teach mankind the lessons that we have learned in our struggle with nature. We have a responsibility to point out the value of this freedom, this freedom to doubt, this freedom to question. We have a responsibility to proclaim the value of this freedom; to teach how doubt is not to be feared but welcomed and discussed; and to demand this freedom as our duty to all coming generations.")]

#zh(id: "S040")[#text("对此，我们应当做些什么？我认为，作为科学家，我们负有特殊的责任。我们有责任把自己在与自然的搏斗中学到的教训传授给人类。我们有责任指出这种自由的价值——怀疑的自由，质问的自由。我们有责任宣扬这种自由的价值，教导人们不必惧怕怀疑，而应当欢迎它、讨论它；我们也有责任要求这种自由，把它作为自己对未来所有世代应尽的义务。")]
